  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 3.083,
      "text": "Some things in the world carry their own identity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 3.083,
      "end": 4.986,
      "text": "A customer is one of those.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 4.986,
      "end": 8.263,
      "text": "You can talk about Maya without mentioning an order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 8.263,
      "end": 11.013,
      "text": "Her customer_id is enough.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 11.013,
      "end": 12.694,
      "text": "That is a strong entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 12.694,
      "end": 17.513,
      "text": "The table has a primary key that does not need another table to make sense.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 17.513,
      "end": 21.0,
      "text": "A weak entity cannot stand on that kind of key alone.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 21.0,
      "end": 25.861,
      "text": "Think of an order line: line one, two copies of Harbor Light.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 25.861,
      "end": 27.5,
      "text": "Line one on which order?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 27.5,
      "end": 29.402,
      "text": "Every order has a line one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 29.402,
      "end": 33.93,
      "text": "The line number only identifies a row when you also know the order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 33.93,
      "end": 35.847,
      "text": "The identity is borrowed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 35.847,
      "end": 37.902,
      "text": "The parent order is the owner.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 37.902,
      "end": 42.486,
      "text": "The child's key is usually the owner's key plus a discriminator.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 42.486,
      "end": 46.097,
      "text": "order_id and line_no together.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 46.097,
      "end": 49.541,
      "text": "That composite key is a feature, not clutter.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 49.541,
      "end": 53.388,
      "text": "If you hide the parent, the child row stops making sense.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 53.388,
      "end": 55.152,
      "text": "Ask that question out loud.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 55.152,
      "end": 58.902,
      "text": "Does this row still name one thing if I erase the parent?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 58.902,
      "end": 62.083,
      "text": "If the answer is no, you have a weak entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 62.083,
      "end": 64.555,
      "text": "Rooms in a building work the same way.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 64.555,
      "end": 66.416,
      "text": "Room 12 in which building?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 66.416,
      "end": 67.75,
      "text": "Seats on a flight.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 67.75,
      "end": 70.458,
      "text": "Seat 14A on which flight number?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 70.458,
      "end": 75.68,
      "text": "Do not invent a random line_id just to pretend the child is strong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 75.68,
      "end": 78.569,
      "text": "You can, and applications sometimes do.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 78.569,
      "end": 85.819,
      "text": "Then you still need a unique pair of order_id and line_no, or you will insert two line ones.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 85.819,
      "end": 88.041,
      "text": "The surrogate hides the weakness.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 88.041,
      "end": 89.527,
      "text": "It does not remove it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 89.527,
      "end": 93.902,
      "text": "On a diagram, a weak entity is often a double box.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 93.902,
      "end": 97.763,
      "text": "The relationship to the owner is often a double diamond.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 97.763,
      "end": 100.638,
      "text": "You do not need the symbols to use the idea.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 100.638,
      "end": 102.722,
      "text": "You need the question about identity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 102.722,
      "end": 107.18,
      "text": "Foreign keys and weak entities overlap but are not the same.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 107.18,
      "end": 112.236,
      "text": "orders.customer_id is a foreign key on a strong entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 112.236,
      "end": 115.722,
      "text": "The order still has order_id of its own.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 115.722,
      "end": 120.527,
      "text": "A weak child uses the parent's key as part of its own primary key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 120.527,
      "end": 122.041,
      "text": "That is a tighter bond.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 122.041,
      "end": 126.194,
      "text": "Deleting the owner without the children is almost always wrong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 126.194,
      "end": 129.027,
      "text": "The children were never independent facts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 129.027,
      "end": 131.5,
      "text": "When you model, list the nouns.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 131.5,
      "end": 134.305,
      "text": "Circle the ones that already have a passport.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 134.305,
      "end": 138.486,
      "text": "Underline the ones that only make sense as a part of something else.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 138.486,
      "end": 140.569,
      "text": "Give the parts a composite key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 140.569,
      "end": 142.694,
      "text": "Give the passports a simple key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 142.694,
      "end": 146.055,
      "text": "Then the schema tells you which rows can travel alone.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 146.055,
      "end": 149.18,
      "text": "Ownership is not the same as a mere pointer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 149.18,
      "end": 152.805,
      "text": "An order points at a customer and still has its own life.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 152.805,
      "end": 154.416,
      "text": "An order line is owned.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 154.416,
      "end": 158.611,
      "text": "You would not archive a line in a warehouse without the order header.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 158.611,
      "end": 161.333,
      "text": "That operational fact is the model.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 161.333,
      "end": 166.097,
      "text": "When teams argue about line_id, ask how they pick up the phone.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 166.097,
      "end": 171.222,
      "text": "Do they say line forty-two globally, or line two on order one-oh-one?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 171.222,
      "end": 173.125,
      "text": "The phone script is the key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 173.125,
      "end": 182.861,
      "text": "History tables sometimes freeze a weak entity into a strong one by giving it a surrogate and copying the parent id as a plain foreign key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 182.861,
      "end": 184.944,
      "text": "That can be right for analytics.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 184.944,
      "end": 187.138,
      "text": "It is a different job than checkout.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 187.138,
      "end": 191.347,
      "text": "Do not let the warehouse rewrite the checkout key without a meeting.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 191.347,
      "end": 195.666,
      "text": "Identifying relationships are the ER phrase for the weak bond.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 195.666,
      "end": 201.444,
      "text": "Non-identifying relationships are foreign keys that are not part of the child's primary key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 201.444,
      "end": 204.236,
      "text": "Use the phrases if your diagram tool does.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 204.236,
      "end": 207.0,
      "text": "Use the identity test if it does not.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 207.0,
      "end": 209.43,
      "text": "Cascade deletes follow ownership.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 209.43,
      "end": 211.583,
      "text": "They do not follow every arrow.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 211.583,
      "end": 214.68,
      "text": "A weak child almost always cascades.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 214.68,
      "end": 217.833,
      "text": "A strong child almost always restricts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 217.833,
      "end": 219.625,
      "text": "Write that next to the box.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 219.625,
      "end": 226.361,
      "text": "Examples besides lines: chapters of a book if you identify them as chapter three of book eleven.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 226.361,
      "end": 230.513,
      "text": "Comments on a review if they are numbered only inside the review.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 230.513,
      "end": 234.583,
      "text": "If comments have public permalink ids, they became strong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 234.583,
      "end": 236.361,
      "text": "The world gets to decide.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 236.361,
      "end": 238.583,
      "text": "Your schema records the decision.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 238.583,
      "end": 241.152,
      "text": "Revisit it when permalinks appear.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 241.152,
      "end": 247.625,
      "text": "Until then, composite keys keep the weakness visible, which is a kindness to the next designer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 247.625,
      "end": 251.68,
      "text": "Strong and weak are not about how important a table feels.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 251.68,
      "end": 255.444,
      "text": "They are about whether a thing can be identified on its own.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 255.444,
      "end": 259.694,
      "text": "Cardinality is how many: one, zero, many.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 259.694,
      "end": 262.125,
      "text": "Weakness is how identity works.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 262.125,
      "end": 264.041,
      "text": "Do not mix those two dials.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 264.041,
      "end": 267.569,
      "text": "A strong entity has its own unique identifier.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 267.569,
      "end": 272.958,
      "text": "A purchase with purchase_id is strong even if it points at a customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 272.958,
      "end": 276.638,
      "text": "Depending on another table for a foreign key is normal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 276.746,
      "end": 282.071,
      "text": "Depending on another table to exist as an identity is the weak case.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 282.071,
      "end": 287.029,
      "text": "A weak entity cannot identify a row with only its own attributes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 287.029,
      "end": 291.876,
      "text": "Its key is usually composite: the parent's key plus something local.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 291.876,
      "end": 298.126,
      "text": "A line on an order might be identified by order_id plus line_number.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 298.126,
      "end": 301.793,
      "text": "Line number three means nothing until you know which order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 301.793,
      "end": 305.751,
      "text": "That is a weak entity, or at least a dependent identity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 305.751,
      "end": 310.265,
      "text": "Beginners mark everything that 'belongs to' something as weak.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 310.265,
      "end": 314.293,
      "text": "An employee has a manager, so employee must be weak.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 314.293,
      "end": 315.057,
      "text": "No.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 315.057,
      "end": 317.904,
      "text": "Employee still has employee_id.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 317.904,
      "end": 320.168,
      "text": "Belonging is a relationship.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 320.168,
      "end": 322.015,
      "text": "Identity is a key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 322.015,
      "end": 331.001,
      "text": "Use a weak design when the child is meaningless and unidentifiable without the parent, and you will never look it up by a surrogate of its own.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 331.001,
      "end": 336.029,
      "text": "Room 12 in building A is not the same as room 12 in building B.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 336.029,
      "end": 343.057,
      "text": "If the business says room numbers restart per building, the room is identified by building plus number.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 343.057,
      "end": 348.418,
      "text": "If every room gets a global room_id, you made it strong on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 348.418,
      "end": 349.654,
      "text": "That is allowed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 349.654,
      "end": 354.39,
      "text": "You are choosing an identifier, not discovering a law of nature.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 354.39,
      "end": 359.584,
      "text": "When you do use a weak entity, the relationship to the parent is identifying.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 359.584,
      "end": 362.543,
      "text": "The parent's key is part of the child's key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 362.543,
      "end": 368.071,
      "text": "Deleting the parent without a plan orphans identity itself, not just a pointer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 368.071,
      "end": 377.89,
      "text": "In an ER diagram, weak entities are often shown with a double rectangle, and the identifying relationship with a double diamond, in Chen style.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 377.89,
      "end": 382.946,
      "text": "Crow's foot sketches may instead show the composite key in the table box.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 382.946,
      "end": 385.557,
      "text": "Pick a notation and stay consistent.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 385.557,
      "end": 391.973,
      "text": "The rare honest case is a child whose natural key is not unique until the parent is included.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 391.973,
      "end": 396.89,
      "text": "The common dishonest case is a regular table you were afraid to give an id.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 396.89,
      "end": 402.196,
      "text": "Give it an id if it is a thing you will query, update, and relate on its own.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 402.196,
      "end": 409.418,
      "text": "Keep it weak if its name is always 'the third line of that order' and never a thing with a passport of its own.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 409.418,
      "end": 413.39,
      "text": "Ask: can I find this row tomorrow without naming the parent?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 413.39,
      "end": 415.321,
      "text": "If yes, it is strong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 415.321,
      "end": 422.265,
      "text": "If no, either add a surrogate and make it strong, or accept the composite and call it weak on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 422.265,
      "end": 424.293,
      "text": "Purpose is the whole lesson.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 424.293,
      "end": 426.932,
      "text": "Weak is a design choice with a cost.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 426.932,
      "end": 430.459,
      "text": "Do not spend it on ordinary belongs-to relationships.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 430.459,
      "end": 431.709,
      "text": "Walk a receipt.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 431.709,
      "end": 435.737,
      "text": "The purchase has purchase_id, a strong entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 435.737,
      "end": 441.209,
      "text": "Each line is line_number one, two, three inside that purchase.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 441.209,
      "end": 444.709,
      "text": "Line number two in another purchase is a different thing.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 444.709,
      "end": 449.987,
      "text": "Identity of a line is purchase_id plus line_number.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 449.987,
      "end": 453.904,
      "text": "That is weak, or identifying dependent, on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 453.904,
      "end": 462.751,
      "text": "Do not give the line a global line_id if the business will only ever say the third line of order 5001.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 462.751,
      "end": 471.418,
      "text": "Do give a global id if warehouse software will move lines between orders and still talk about line 88901.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 471.418,
      "end": 474.251,
      "text": "That second world made the line strong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 474.251,
      "end": 485.654,
      "text": "A dependent person on an employee benefits form is the textbook weak example: name plus employee_id, because dependents are not issued employee numbers.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 485.654,
      "end": 491.654,
      "text": "If your company later issues every dependent a person_id, they stopped being weak.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 491.654,
      "end": 497.696,
      "text": "The ER mark changed because the identifiers changed, not because cardinality changed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 497.696,
      "end": 500.321,
      "text": "One employee still has many dependents.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 500.321,
      "end": 502.112,
      "text": "That was always one-to-many.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 502.112,
      "end": 504.348,
      "text": "Weakness was only about the key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 504.348,
      "end": 512.543,
      "text": "When not to use weak: any table you will load, search, and relate without reciting the parent id every time.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 512.543,
      "end": 519.376,
      "text": "Users, products, invoices with invoice_id, shipments with tracking numbers.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 519.376,
      "end": 520.626,
      "text": "Those are strong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 520.626,
      "end": 526.598,
      "text": "Mislabeling them weak clutters the diagram with double lines that mean nothing in SQL.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 526.598,
      "end": 529.459,
      "text": "SQL still wants a PRIMARY KEY either way.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 529.459,
      "end": 533.696,
      "text": "The weak case just makes that key composite and identifying.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 533.696,
      "end": 537.098,
      "text": "Choose with the find-this-tomorrow test, then draw.",
      "slide": ""
    }
  ]
}
